ort and use it to update the world model. Helpful optional prefixes are `World model:`, `Goal model:`, `Action model:`, `Recent findings:`, `Open questions:`, `Plan:`, and `Cross-level notes:`.\nWhen calling `python`, emit exactly the tool-call format shown elsewhere in this prompt for this model. Use only that format; do not add markdown fences, prose wrappers, or alternate tool-call syntax. Do not quote or place tool-call markup inside explanatory text; when you decide to call the tool, emit the tool call itself.\nIf you use MOUSE, include integer row and col arguments.\nEFFICIENCY BUDGET \u2014 your score on each level is (baseline_actions / your_actions)^2, so every wasted action costs you quadratically.\nLevel 2: you have used 30 of about 54 target actions so far.", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "THINKING", "content": "After SPACE, the cup rotated:\n- White cup at [[29, 50], [29, 52], [46, 52], [46, 44]] - opens DOWN (vertical shape at rows 29-46, cols 44-52)\n- Red squares at (29, 38), (29, 47), and (35, 44)\n- Green frame at [[32, 38], [32, 49], [34, 49], [34, 38]] - rows 32-34, cols 38-49\nThe cup is now vertical, opening DOWN. The red square at (35, 44) is at row 35, col 44, which is below the cup's bottom at row 46. Wait, that doesn't make sense. Let me re-examine.\nThe cup's boundary is [[29, 50], [29, 52], [46, 52], [46, 44]], which is a vertical shape at rows 29-46, cols 44-52. The opening is at the bottom (row 46), so it opens DOWN.\nThe red squares are at (29, 38), (29, 47), and (35, 44). The red square at (35, 44) is at row 35, col 44, which is inside the cup's vertical range (rows 29-46) and at the left edge of the cup (col 44).\nThe green frame is at rows 32-34, cols 38-49. The red square at (29, 47) is at row 29, col 47, which is above the green frame (rows 32-34). The red square at (35, 44) is at row 35, col 44, which is below the green frame (rows 32-34).\nSince the cup opens DOWN, I should try moving DOWN to get the red squares 